diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b618978
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+## Deployment (Single Server with Kamal)
+
+Fizzy includes a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration (`config/deploy.yml` and `.kamal/secrets`) for deploying everything in a single container on one Linux server with SQLite, automatic SSL via `kamal-proxy`, persistent storage, and in-container Solid Queue background jobs.
+
+### 1. Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server reachable over SSH (Kamal installs Docker automatically during `kamal setup` if needed)
+- A domain name with DNS pointing to your server's IP address (for automatic Let's Encrypt SSL)
+- An SMTP mail server (needed for magic-link sign-in and notification emails)
+- Docker installed locally to build the container image (pushed via Kamal's built-in `localhost:5555` registry)
+
+### 2. Configure `config/deploy.yml`
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` with your server, hostname, and mail server:
+
+- `servers.web`: replace `192.0.2.1` with your server's IP address or SSH hostname.
+- `proxy.host`: replace `fizzy.example.com` with your domain name (this also sets `APP_HOST` via the YAML anchor).
+- `builder.arch`: change `amd64` to `arm64` if your server is ARM-based.
+- `env.clear`: set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, and `SMTP_USERNAME` (leave `SMTP_USERNAME` blank if your relay does not require authentication).
+
+### 3. Configure Secrets
+
+`.kamal/secrets` reads `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `SMTP_PASSWORD`, `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`, and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` from environment variables by default (or you can point `.kamal/secrets` to a password manager or untracked file).
+
+Generate a `SECRET_KEY_BASE`:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails secret
+```
+
+Optionally generate VAPID keys for browser Web Push notifications:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'k = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{k.public_key}\nVAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{k.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Export the secrets in your shell (or configure `.kamal/secrets` to fetch them):
+
+```sh
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="..."
+export SMTP_PASSWORD="..."
+export VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY="..."
+export VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY="..."
+```
+
+### 4. Deploy
+
+Commit your changes to `config/deploy.yml` (Kamal builds from git `HEAD`) and run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Once finished, visit `https://your-host` to create your first account. Subsequent deploys only require:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+### Data Persistence & Background Jobs
+
+- **Database & Uploads**: All SQLite databases (`production.sqlite3`, `production_cable.sqlite3`, `production_cache.sqlite3`, `production_queue.sqlite3`) and local Active Storage uploads live under `/rails/storage`, backed by the `fizzy_storage` Docker volume so data survives deploys.
+- **Background Jobs**: Solid Queue runs inside Puma in the same container by default (`config/puma.rb`).
+- **SSL**: `kamal-proxy` terminates TLS using Let's Encrypt and forwards requests to the app over port 80.
